# Formatters must not touch CoDD's canonical documents.
#
# Why: a requirement unit is a Markdown TABLE ROW. A formatter that only
# re-aligns table pipes changes no meaning, so review will not catch it — but
# it breaks byte-identity between the human-approved original and the document
# CoDD reconciles against, and every check stays green while it happens.
# Observed in the field: 440 lines of a requirements table silently reformatted
# by `npx prettier --write .`.
#
# This file is written unconditionally by `codd init` because the artifact at
# risk (Markdown under docs/) is language-independent: any repository can
# adopt a Markdown formatter regardless of its primary language. It is inert
# in a repository that does not use Prettier.

# CoDD canon — the requirement documents CoDD parses
docs/requirements/

# Reference copies of upstream/source material (see codd.yaml). Keep these
# OUT of docs/requirements/: every *.md under docs/requirements/ is discovered
# and counted as requirements, so a copy placed there double-counts silently.
docs/source/

# CoDD config, scan output and reports
{{config_dir}}/

# Generated / vendored
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
